---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import IndustryControlFlow from "../components/diagrams/IndustryControlFlow.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Healthcare | BeaconGuard for Regulated Healthcare AI Actions"
  description="BeaconGuard is the initial-market authorization layer for healthcare AI workflows: Request Admission before provider invocation and Result-to-Action before enterprise effect. AI output remains untrusted; the EHR remains authoritative."
>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <p class="section-label">INITIAL MARKET</p>
    <h1>
      Control AI-assisted healthcare actions before they affect clinical
      workflows.
    </h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Healthcare is BeaconGuard’s primary initial market. The lead wedge is
      AI-assisted patient communication—governing whether outreach may be
      invoked and whether a declared send, queue, or status update may proceed.
      BeaconGuard also applies to documentation assistance and care-operations
      pathways. AI output remains an untrusted proposal. BeaconGuard authorizes;
      the application executes; the EHR and other systems of record remain
      authoritative.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Healthcare governed AI transaction</h2>
    <p>
      Reaching an AI provider is not the complete governed outcome. Enterprise
      effect still requires independent Result-to-Action Authorization of the
      declared intended action under the Active Verified Release.
    </p>
    <IndustryControlFlow industry="healthcare" />
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Dual authorization points</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Request Admission Authorization</strong> — may the application
        invoke the AI provider?
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Result-to-Action Authorization</strong> — may the declared
        intended enterprise action proceed?
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Runtime outcomes are <strong>ALLOW</strong> or <strong>DENY</strong> only.
      Provider success is not enterprise authorization. Review does not convert
      a recorded DENY into ALLOW.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Existing healthcare systems remain in place</h2>
    <p>
      BeaconGuard does not replace the EHR, privacy office, clinical governance
      process, care-management platform, or other systems of record. Those
      systems remain authoritative for clinical and operational state. Customer
      governance retains clinical, privacy, and compliance judgment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Healthcare scenarios</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Illustrative controlled example.</strong> The lead scenario is
      patient communication. Documentation assistance and care-operations
      pathways are secondary illustrations of the same governed transaction
      pattern: admission, optional provider result, declared action, action
      authorization, and evidence — without claiming clinical correctness or
      production healthcare validation.
    </p>
    <div class="scenario-grid">
      <div class="scenario-card scenario-card--lead">
        <p class="section-label">LEAD SCENARIO</p>
        <h3>Patient communication</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Existing workflow:</strong> Care operations drafts patient
          outreach or follow-up messaging with AI assistance.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Request Admission:</strong> ALLOW only when pathway, role,
          trust, and freshness satisfy the Active Verified Release.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI-Generated Result:</strong> Proposed message content —
          untrusted proposal.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Intended action examples:</strong> Send outreach, queue
          follow-up, update communication status.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Result-to-Action:</strong> Independent ALLOW or DENY for the
          declared action. DENY prevents enterprise effect.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Authoritative system:</strong> Care operations and EHR remain
          systems of record.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Clinical documentation assistance</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Existing workflow:</strong> Clinician or scribe tooling
          requests AI assistance for documentation drafting.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Request Admission:</strong> DENY when required privacy
          approval, pathway, or trust context is absent.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI-Generated Result:</strong> Draft documentation text —
          untrusted proposal, not clinical authority.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Intended action examples:</strong> Insert draft into chart
          workflow, submit for clinician review, update documentation state.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Result-to-Action:</strong> Authorizes the declared use of the
          draft — not medical correctness of the content.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Authoritative system:</strong> EHR and clinical documentation
          systems remain authoritative.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Care-operations workflow</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Existing workflow:</strong> Operational summarization or
          routing over PHI-bearing records to support care operations.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Request Admission:</strong> DENY for unapproved pathways,
          stale or replayed requests, or missing required context.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI-Generated Result:</strong> Proposed summary or routing
          recommendation — untrusted proposal.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Intended action examples:</strong> Route a case, update
          operational status, create a follow-up task.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Result-to-Action:</strong> ALLOW permits the application to
          execute the declared action; DENY hard-stops enterprise effect.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Authoritative system:</strong> Care-management platforms and
          the EHR remain authoritative.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>What BeaconGuard does not claim</h2>
    <ul class="bg-nonclaim-list">
      <li>Clinical correctness or medical certification of AI output</li>
      <li>Replacement of clinician judgment or privacy-office decisions</li>
      <li>Replacement of the EHR or other systems of record</li>
      <li>Independent HIPAA certification or legal compliance attestation</li>
      <li>Customer healthcare production validation or production-ready status</li>
      <li>Authorization of model content as semantic truth</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a
        class="btn-primary"
        href="mailto:architecture@beaconguardassurance.com?subject=Healthcare%20Workflow%20Review"
      >
        Request a Healthcare Workflow Review
      </a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/canonical-workflow">Review Governed Transaction</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/docs/architecture">Review System Architecture</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
